# Loaded by Vite only in "desktop" mode (`vite --mode desktop` / `vite build --mode desktop`),
# which `tauri.conf.json`'s beforeDevCommand/beforeBuildCommand run via the `dev:desktop`/
# `build:desktop` npm scripts. Layers on top of `.env`/`.env.production` - only the override
# below belongs here (D4).
#
# The local-first engine is on for the desktop build only, by design (D4). The Tauri build stores
# its local copy in a SQLCipher-encrypted on-disk database (`src-tauri/src/db.rs`); the web build
# stays online-only rather than ship a partly-offline experience through browser storage.
VITE_LOCAL_FIRST=true

# The local-lock PIN feature stays dormant on the desktop build too (BUG-31): setting a PIN ran a
# bare `PRAGMA key` against the already-populated plaintext SQLite file and corrupted it. Do not
# set VITE_LOCAL_PIN=true until db_open keys the DB from the OS keychain on a store encrypted from
# creation. Left unset here on purpose; the flag defaults off.

# The desktop installer is built in CI (`.github/workflows/release.yml`), where the git-ignored
# `.env` does not exist - so the hosted backend URL has to live here, in the one env file the
# Tauri build always reads. Without these, `VITE_API_URL` falls back to the localhost default in
# `src/utils/apiPaths.ts` and every shipped install fails to reach the server ("Network Error").
# Tauri's CSP (`tauri.conf.json`) pins `connect-src` to `https://api.corvale.app` (SEC-43), and
# index.html's CSP is built from `VITE_API_ORIGIN`. If the API origin ever changes, update all
# three together: `VITE_API_URL`, `VITE_API_ORIGIN`, and `tauri.conf.json`'s `connect-src`.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.corvale.app/api/v1
VITE_API_ORIGIN=https://api.corvale.app
VITE_DOCS_URL=https://docs.corvale.app

# Must match the *production* backend's `OFFLINE_GRANT_PRIVATE_KEY` (public half, newlines as
# literal `\n`). Without it the "sign in once, then offline forever" path fails closed - online
# sign-in still works, but a relaunch with no network won't restore the session. Verify this is
# the production keypair, not a dev one, before releasing.
VITE_OFFLINE_GRANT_PUBLIC_KEY=-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nMFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAE8s8D9YhX9MSPJia+hZB1KXh1CRKb\nnm1CBTv39I7iVVnAxfJ06qkpdj2iTPz+pXSax7jRo6MEWqRuoi2Nw9Dslg==\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
